## Breed scanner

The breed scanner's image-recognition model (based on EfficientNet-B0, pretrained on ImageNet and published with the PyTorch torchvision library under the BSD 3-Clause licence) was trained by AxiomaraGames on:

- the **Oxford-IIIT Pet Dataset** by O. M. Parkhi, A. Vedaldi, A. Zisserman and C. V. Jawahar (Visual Geometry Group, University of Oxford), used under the [Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/): https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/pets/
- photos of cat breeds from **Wikimedia Commons**, each used under its own free licence (Creative Commons or public domain).

The photos themselves are not part of the app; only the model learnt from them is. No photographer or dataset author endorses the app.

## Breed and care information

The breed profiles, guides, food list and symptom checker were written for the app, based on generally accepted guidance from cat welfare and veterinary organisations such as International Cat Care, the American Association of Feline Practitioners (AAFP), the Cornell Feline Health Center, the ASPCA Animal Poison Control Center and the breed standards of the major cat registries (TICA, CFA, GCCF). These organisations are not affiliated with the app and have not reviewed or endorsed it.

